  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Pinède is a 3-star campsite with 200 large pitches in a pine wood on the Le Brusc peninsula, in Six-Fours-les-Plages. Pitches are either fully shaded under the pines or partly shaded. The sea and the first coves are 1 km away, the sandy beach, shops and village of Le Brusc 1.8 km. On site: a baker every morning, a snack bar, a playground and a petanque court. The campsite is open from June to September.</p>

      <h2>The dog rule</h2>
      <p>The campsite's own website says dogs are allowed on a leash with an up-to-date health certificate, except category 1 and 2 dogs. Its price list shows a €3 dog supplement, while the Provence Méditerranée tourist office listing (updated April 2026) shows €2 for a dog outside categories 1 and 2. Both figures come from official sources: confirm which one applies when you book.</p>
      <p>The highlight: 300 m from the campsite, the management lets campers use a 4,000 m² wooded plot to run and play with their dogs.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask reception where the 4,000 m² wooded plot is, 300 m from the campsite and kept for campers' dogs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>From Le Brusc, the tourist office mentions 70 km of mountain-bike trails, walking routes and a riding club nearby, as well as the Île du Gaou, facing the Embiez islands, for picnics under the pines and access to coves.</p>
    </div>

